00:01:49.970 --> 00:01:51.730
- So maybe a couple of quick questions.

00:01:51.730 --> 00:01:55.723
Why is today National
Constitution Day, September 17th?

00:01:56.830 --> 00:01:59.027
- So September 17th, 1787

00:01:59.027 --> 00:02:01.320
was the day the Constitution was signed

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:04.290
in Independence Hall in Philadelphia.

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:08.593
It wasn't made a national
holiday, until 2004.

00:02:09.664 --> 00:02:10.890
There've been precursors of it,

00:02:10.890 --> 00:02:14.370
in 1940, there was something
called Citizenship Day,

00:02:14.370 --> 00:02:17.150
but basically ever since a law in 2004,

00:02:17.150 --> 00:02:19.090
sponsored by Senator Robert Byrd,

00:02:19.090 --> 00:02:21.450
the U.S has recognized the anniversary

00:02:21.450 --> 00:02:23.583
of the day when the
Constitution was signed.

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:25.420
- Makes a lot of sense.

