00:23:57.170 --> 00:23:58.003
Sal just ask,

00:23:58.003 --> 00:24:00.320
and we did have a podcast on the ERA

00:24:00.320 --> 00:24:02.830
and what it would mean a few months ago.

00:24:02.830 --> 00:24:04.990
And as usual, it's complicated,

00:24:04.990 --> 00:24:06.470
people disagree about what it would mean.

00:24:06.470 --> 00:24:08.640
But the progressive scholar thought

00:24:08.640 --> 00:24:12.840
it would be a strong basis
for reproductive rights.

00:24:12.840 --> 00:24:15.420
Justice Ginsburg has
argued that restrictions

00:24:15.420 --> 00:24:18.010
on a woman's right to choose violate

00:24:18.010 --> 00:24:21.620
not the right to privacy of male doctors

00:24:21.620 --> 00:24:23.210
but the right of equality of women

00:24:23.210 --> 00:24:24.950
whose life choices are constrained

00:24:24.950 --> 00:24:27.923
by not being able to choose to be,

00:24:29.960 --> 00:24:33.070
caregivers or not based on
their own individual choice.

00:24:33.070 --> 00:24:37.920
So it might be used to argue
for a right of reproduction

00:24:37.920 --> 00:24:41.070
and to argue to strike down
restrictions on that way.

00:24:41.070 --> 00:24:45.793
Others say that it would
require, for example,

00:24:47.166 --> 00:24:50.460
LGBTQ people to have transgender bathrooms

00:24:50.460 --> 00:24:54.850
and would forbid bathrooms
that are marked for people

00:24:54.850 --> 00:24:57.070
who identify as male or female.

00:24:57.070 --> 00:25:00.320
Others disagree about that.

00:25:00.320 --> 00:25:04.360
Others say that it would
allow courts to root out

00:25:04.360 --> 00:25:08.660
unconscious gender bias
as a form of a violation

00:25:08.660 --> 00:25:10.610
of discrimination on the basis of sex

00:25:10.610 --> 00:25:12.690
rather than intentional discrimination.

00:25:12.690 --> 00:25:15.750
Which so far the Supreme Court
has held is the only kind of

00:25:15.750 --> 00:25:17.040
discrimination that's forbidden.

00:25:17.040 --> 00:25:19.020
Now, you can argue all of this

00:25:19.020 --> 00:25:20.367
round or flat as the lawyer say,

00:25:20.367 --> 00:25:23.620
and you could say that since
the Constitution already

00:25:23.620 --> 00:25:25.700
guarantees equal protection of the law,

00:25:25.700 --> 00:25:28.080
and since the Supreme Court just last term

00:25:28.080 --> 00:25:30.760
in a six to three decision
by justice Gorsuch

00:25:30.760 --> 00:25:34.230
held the title seven of the
Civil Rights Act of 1964.

00:25:34.230 --> 00:25:36.980
And it's forbidding
discrimination on the basis of sex

00:25:36.980 --> 00:25:38.630
covers not only gender discrimination,

00:25:38.630 --> 00:25:41.960
but also discrimination on
the basis of LGBTQ status,

00:25:41.960 --> 00:25:44.020
that an ERA wouldn't add all that much

00:25:44.020 --> 00:25:46.720
to that existing statutory protection.

00:25:46.720 --> 00:25:48.360
The final thing I'll say

00:25:48.360 --> 00:25:50.300
when you ask a great
Constitutional question

00:25:50.300 --> 00:25:53.300
there's always a technical
answer that you can't know

00:25:53.300 --> 00:25:55.080
unless you've heard the
arguments on both sides.

00:25:55.080 --> 00:25:57.810
And I didn't know this until the podcasts.

00:25:57.810 --> 00:25:59.760
Justice Ginsburg when she was an advocate

00:25:59.760 --> 00:26:01.220
arguing before the Supreme Court

00:26:01.220 --> 00:26:03.200
said that discrimination
on the basis of sex

00:26:03.200 --> 00:26:05.790
should be treated just a
skeptically under the law

00:26:05.790 --> 00:26:08.180
as discrimination on the basis of race.

00:26:08.180 --> 00:26:11.010
And the lawyers test for that
is called strict scrutiny.

00:26:11.010 --> 00:26:13.830
And it means that any burdens on the right

00:26:13.830 --> 00:26:15.380
have to be necessary to achieve

00:26:15.380 --> 00:26:16.990
a compelling governmental interest.

00:26:16.990 --> 00:26:19.310
The Supreme Court never quite adopted

00:26:19.310 --> 00:26:20.560
Justice Ginsburg standard

00:26:20.560 --> 00:26:22.560
and in the Virginia
Military Institute case

00:26:22.560 --> 00:26:23.550
which she wrote,

00:26:23.550 --> 00:26:26.510
which struck down separately
equal military academies

00:26:26.510 --> 00:26:27.490
for men and women.

00:26:27.490 --> 00:26:30.620
The court adopts said
that gender discrimination

00:26:30.620 --> 00:26:32.670
should be treated nearly as skeptically,

00:26:32.670 --> 00:26:34.280
as discrimination on the basis of race.

00:26:34.280 --> 00:26:37.060
We needed an exceedingly
persuasive justification

00:26:37.060 --> 00:26:40.220
and ERA would unequivocally guarantee

00:26:40.220 --> 00:26:43.040
strict scrutiny and require
a compelling interest

00:26:43.040 --> 00:26:44.680
for gender discrimination.

00:26:44.680 --> 00:26:45.530
And in that sense,

00:26:45.530 --> 00:26:48.560
it would certainly put
discrimination on the basis of sex

00:26:48.560 --> 00:26:50.430
on the same legal plan,

00:26:50.430 --> 00:26:52.730
there's discrimination
on the basis of rights.

00:26:53.793 --> 00:26:54.650
