meant by Amendments?

00:27:10.070 --> 00:27:10.920
I feel so lost.

00:27:10.920 --> 00:27:14.580
So that's another thing Amendment
literally means to amend,

00:27:14.580 --> 00:27:17.270
to add, to modify,
anything you would add to,

00:27:17.270 --> 00:27:19.860
anything you would amend to
my explanation of Amendments.

00:27:19.860 --> 00:27:24.393
- I just would add synonyms change, alter,

00:27:28.600 --> 00:27:30.240
put in, add.

00:27:30.240 --> 00:27:31.700
I think that was one of your words,

00:27:31.700 --> 00:27:35.700
change, alter, add is
what an Amendment is.

00:27:35.700 --> 00:27:38.560
So the original Constitution,

00:27:38.560 --> 00:27:41.920
remember we said, didn't
have a bill of rights.

00:27:41.920 --> 00:27:44.940
So the first 10 changes
to the Constitution

00:27:44.940 --> 00:27:45.773
are called Amendments.

00:27:45.773 --> 00:27:47.000
The first Amendment says,

00:27:47.000 --> 00:27:48.320
Congress shall make no law

00:27:48.320 --> 00:27:51.530
abridging the freedom of
speech or of the press.

00:27:51.530 --> 00:27:53.980
And you had to amend or
change the Constitution

00:27:53.980 --> 00:27:55.660
to guarantee that right of free speech.

00:27:55.660 --> 00:27:58.360
Cause it didn't appear in
the original Constitution.

00:27:58.360 --> 00:28:00.440
So an Amendment is the
change to the Constitution,

00:28:00.440 --> 00:28:03.010
but it's so it's actually
quite a deep question.

00:28:03.010 --> 00:28:05.280
Of course, as all of
your great questions are

00:28:05.280 --> 00:28:07.690
because in changing the Constitution,

00:28:07.690 --> 00:28:10.480
you're incorporating a principle into it

00:28:10.480 --> 00:28:13.190
that has just as much weight
as the original principles.

00:28:13.190 --> 00:28:17.330
So in some cases you have to
read the original Constitution

00:28:17.330 --> 00:28:19.490
in light of its subsequent Amendments.

00:28:19.490 --> 00:28:21.920
And to give the most important example,

00:28:21.920 --> 00:28:24.720
the original Constitution
only bound Congress.

00:28:24.720 --> 00:28:25.980
It didn't bound the states.

00:28:25.980 --> 00:28:27.240
It says Congress shall make no law,

00:28:27.240 --> 00:28:29.190
abridging free speech it didn't say

00:28:29.190 --> 00:28:30.800
the state shall make no law.

00:28:30.800 --> 00:28:33.230
The 14th Amendment to the Constitution

00:28:33.230 --> 00:28:36.740
was intended to apply all
of those original Amendments

00:28:37.880 --> 00:28:39.920
against the states as well as congress

00:28:39.920 --> 00:28:42.730
through the privileges
or immunities clauses,

00:28:42.730 --> 00:28:45.250
it's called the Doctrine of Incorporation

00:28:45.250 --> 00:28:46.630
and the bottom line friends again,

00:28:46.630 --> 00:28:47.980
I know it's getting technical again,

00:28:47.980 --> 00:28:49.030
but it's usually important.

00:28:49.030 --> 00:28:50.070
Just think of this.

00:28:50.070 --> 00:28:52.380
After the 14th Amendment
passed after the civil war,

00:28:52.380 --> 00:28:54.720
the states are just as prohibited from

00:28:54.720 --> 00:28:56.730
infringing free speeches congress was

00:28:56.730 --> 00:28:58.900
before the 14th Amendment they were free

00:28:58.900 --> 00:29:01.770
to infringe free speech
in Federal Constitution.

00:29:01.770 --> 00:29:03.010
So that's what an Amendment is.

00:29:03.010 --> 00:29:05.600
And any time you wanna
change the Constitution,

00:29:05.600 --> 00:29:07.090
at least changes the text,

00:29:07.090 --> 00:29:09.360
you have to pass an Amendment.

00:29:09.360 --> 00:29:10.910
- Yeah, it's, you're definitely adding

00:29:10.910 --> 00:29:12.270
to the text of the Constitution,

00:29:12.270 --> 00:29:14.380
I guess you could, or to the overall text,

00:29:14.380 --> 00:29:16.200
I guess you could say,
cause you're adding more

00:29:16.200 --> 00:29:18.450
and it could be a change to your point

00:29:18.450 --> 00:29:20.460
with the 14th Amendment or
it could be clarification,

00:29:20.460 --> 00:29:23.590
you know, the first
Amendment doesn't contradict

00:29:23.590 --> 00:29:26.240
the rest of the Constitution
to Madison's point,

00:29:26.240 --> 00:29:27.660
but it makes it very clear

00:29:27.660 --> 00:29:30.040
that you have the right to free speech.

