how when you just take
the time to sit down

00:33:22.820 --> 00:33:24.430
and have a thoughtful conversation

00:33:24.430 --> 00:33:26.230
with people of different perspectives.

00:33:26.230 --> 00:33:28.620
And I encourage people to do exactly

00:33:28.620 --> 00:33:30.440
what I'm encouraging all of you to do now,

00:33:30.440 --> 00:33:32.560
which is to set aside your
political disagreements,

00:33:32.560 --> 00:33:34.940
cause we're not gonna persuade
each other about politics,

00:33:34.940 --> 00:33:39.070
but to have enough
humility to learn deeply

00:33:39.070 --> 00:33:41.840
about something you don't already
know the answer to namely,

00:33:41.840 --> 00:33:43.460
what does the text say?

00:33:43.460 --> 00:33:45.130
What were the original founding stories

00:33:45.130 --> 00:33:46.250
that gave rise to it?

00:33:46.250 --> 00:33:47.900
What is the Supreme Court said?

00:33:47.900 --> 00:33:50.640
What are the philosophical arguments

00:33:50.640 --> 00:33:53.120
that undergird these principles

00:33:53.120 --> 00:33:55.560
and how should they apply in
light of changing technologies?

00:33:55.560 --> 00:33:58.580
These are such hard and rich questions

00:33:58.580 --> 00:34:00.290
that you end up after
it's spending some time

00:34:00.290 --> 00:34:01.410
thinking about it.

00:34:01.410 --> 00:34:03.850
I always end up in a surprising place

00:34:03.850 --> 00:34:05.530
having learned something
that I didn't know before.

00:34:05.530 --> 00:34:07.090
So I am very encouraged

00:34:07.090 --> 00:34:09.570
that as long as we continue
to create the spaces,

00:34:09.570 --> 00:34:11.450
the platforms like you're creating Sal,

00:34:11.450 --> 00:34:13.750
like we're trying to create
The Constitution Center

00:34:13.750 --> 00:34:15.330
where people can just take the time

00:34:15.330 --> 00:34:17.290
to have this civil dialogues.

00:34:17.290 --> 00:34:20.250
I am optimistic that the U.S Constitution

00:34:20.250 --> 00:34:23.630
will continue to provide a
framework for civil dialogue

00:34:23.630 --> 00:34:26.170
and that neither we the
people will continue

00:34:26.170 --> 00:34:28.043
to rule ourselves by reason.

00:34:29.140 --> 00:34:30.810
- Now well, that too is very inspiring.

00:34:30.810 --> 00:34:32.400
And I got to say, cause I've
had the luxury of, you know,

00:34:32.400 --> 00:34:34.080
we've done this in a
few Khan Academy videos

00:34:34.080 --> 00:34:35.830
and National Constitution Center videos,

00:34:35.830 --> 00:34:38.080
where we went into some of
the Supreme Court cases.

00:34:38.080 --> 00:34:40.230
And, you know, a lot of
these cases I entered in

00:34:40.230 --> 00:34:41.970
like surely they would vote this way.

00:34:41.970 --> 00:34:43.530
Any reasonable person would,

00:34:43.530 --> 00:34:46.070
but when you actually go into the details,

00:34:46.070 --> 00:34:47.220
the intricacies of the case, you're like,

00:34:47.220 --> 00:34:48.760
Oh, I guess they do have a good point.

00:34:48.760 --> 00:34:51.500
And oftentimes you switch your position

00:34:51.500 --> 00:34:52.940
when you really learn what's going on.

00:34:52.940 --> 00:34:54.720
So yeah, I love that call to just

00:34:54.720 --> 00:34:56.100
double, triple click on things.

00:34:56.100 --> 00:34:57.400
Don't just take it, you know,

00:34:57.400 --> 00:34:58.800
just don't look at things

00:34:58.800 --> 00:35:00.690
and get outraged as quickly as possible.

00:35:00.690 --> 00:35:03.500
You know, try to exercise some humility

00:35:03.500 --> 00:35:05.100
to understand the other side.

00:35:05.100 --> 00:35:08.820
So Jeff, thank you so much
happy Constitution Day.

00:35:08.820 --> 00:35:12.610
And I think this was a real
treat on Constitution Day.

00:35:12.610 --> 00:35:14.700
- Happy Constitution Day to everyone.

00:35:14.700 --> 00:35:16.090
So excited to learn with you

00:35:16.090 --> 00:35:18.300
and check out the
Interactive Constitution,

00:35:18.300 --> 00:35:21.030
pick an Amendment or a pause
that you didn't know about

00:35:21.030 --> 00:35:22.830
digging deep and enjoy the learning.

00:35:22.830 --> 00:35:26.100
It's just such a joy to be able
to learn and grow together.

00:35:26.100 --> 00:35:27.110
Happy Constitution Day.

00:35:27.110 --> 00:35:28.330
- Right, thanks.

00:35:28.330 --> 00:35:29.163
Thanks Jeff.

00:35:30.230 --> 00:35:31.960
Well, thanks everyone for joining,

00:35:31.960 --> 00:35:33.970
as always really fun conversation,

00:35:33.970 --> 00:35:35.350
I highly recommend going to

00:35:35.350 --> 00:35:38.010
The National Constitution
Center's website,

00:35:38.010 --> 00:35:39.570
look at The Interactive Constitution,

00:35:39.570 --> 00:35:40.480
attend those classes.

00:35:40.480 --> 00:35:42.980
You might see me as one of your classmates

00:35:42.980 --> 00:35:45.160
in some of those classes cause I think

00:35:45.160 --> 00:35:47.080
not only will it help
you appreciate history

00:35:47.080 --> 00:35:50.660
and how law and nations are constituted,

00:35:50.660 --> 00:35:53.640
but it'll actually build your
critical thinking skills.

00:35:53.640 --> 00:35:55.260
And I actually think the more people

00:35:55.260 --> 00:35:58.510
that dig into these issues
at a higher level of depth,

00:35:58.510 --> 00:36:01.130
I actually think that can
help the polarization problem.

00:36:01.130 --> 00:36:03.050
Cause you could still
disagree with the other side,

00:36:03.050 --> 00:36:06.640
but you can start to understand
some of the reasoning

00:36:06.640 --> 00:36:09.210
for why a reasonable person
might come to a conclusion

00:36:09.210 --> 00:36:10.380
that you don't.

00:36:10.380 --> 00:36:13.410
So with that, thank you
so much for joining.

00:36:13.410 --> 00:36:16.350
Let's see, I think the next show

00:36:16.350 --> 00:36:18.660
is going to be on Tuesday of next week.

00:36:18.660 --> 00:36:20.420
So have a good weekend.

00:36:20.420 --> 00:36:21.400
See you all.

